{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Cevjp2WqKHRCEB1Wvgxax","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NEp2TMRHwQxJtdXGsdBWqw","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"arguments_json":"{\"response\":\"Returned the completed Independent Plan Review as Markdown with the seven required sections. Summary of the analysis follows; full text delivered above.\\n\\n# Independent Plan Review\\n\\nBased on the returned code (planner.py, contract.py, intent.py, errors.py, settings.py, test_planner.py, test_agent_loop.py), the plan, and the current contract. Authority for REQUIRED/MATERIAL/DEFAULTABLE is already resolved in contract.py (shim removed, structured conditional_material read, no prose parsing), narrowing the review to the plan's additions.\\n\\n## Approach challenges\\n1. Blanket bad_request→TerminalError conflates planner-construction defects with faithfully-passed user-supplied bad numeric IDs; combined with the plan's deliberate non-validation of caller IDs (out_of_scope), a user typo becomes an operational crash on the live emitter (POC_CONTRACT_V0.3_SPEC error boundary; C1).\\n2. The planner still repairs (headcount/non-teaching scope cleanup + normalization), so safety depends on normalization being total over the pinned vocabularies or crashes become common.\\n3. \\\"Exactly one directory record\\\" turns common multi-match single-school intents into clarifications — a reliability trade unquantified; live behaviour untested (ADR-016).\\n\\n## Requirement coverage gaps\\n- VC-POC-09/10 \\\"at least one filter beyond sector default\\\" (OD-07) unaddressed; only-defaults dispatches then crashes.\\n- No whitelisting of free-form intent.filters against additionalProperties:false schemas → stray key crashes.\\n- Silent drop of requested_metrics for no-selector questions unstated.\\n- teaching staff→teaching_fte alias now co-owned by rules.md and planner with no drift check (blind Q5).\\n\\n## Unsupported architecture assumptions\\n- Runtime input-catalog load for static vocabularies adds non-determinism vs pinned registry/snapshot (ADR-016).\\n- Assumes client exposes catalog (only school_directory/fetch_evidence evidenced) — missing evidence.\\n- Assumes planner is production path and golden baseline exercises it (run.py not returned) — missing evidence.\\n- \\\"Deterministic from intent\\\" contradicted by request_scope_problem(deps.user_question).\\n\\n## Contract testability and achievability\\n- All gates are exit-code-only with -k filters that can pass vacuously (no min-count/named-test assertions).\\n- \\\"Fail closed\\\"/\\\"fail before dispatch\\\" outcome type unspecified (TerminalError vs Clarify vs Unsupported).\\n- bad-request-failure universally quantified but true only under the stub; 99999 empty-success diverges live (C1).\\n- O-8 xfail freeze is an implicit, unstated requirement; also two-path divergence unsurfaced.\\n- VC-POC-03→ratios routing authority unnamed (pinned-policy-authority risk).\\n- \\\"catalog-backed allowed values where available\\\" is soft/gameable.\\n\\n## Blind findings disposition\\nResolved: Q1, Q4, Q8 (planner logic), largely Q7. Partial: Q3 (planner fixes conditional distance, agent path unchanged/divergence unsurfaced), Q6 (zero/multi added, absent-ID now crashes). Unanswered: Q2 user-bad-ID sub-case, Q5 divergence test, live directory verification.\\n\\n## Falsifiable questions for reconciliation\\nTen questions listed covering: user-bad-ID crash intent; normalization totality; VC-POC-09/10 constraint; filter whitelisting; VC-POC-03 routing authority; planner live-path wiring; deps.user_question determinism; runtime vs pinned catalog; typed outcome for fail-closed cases; and whether freezing the O-8 agent-loop bug is deliberate.\\n\\nNo pass/fail, materiality, or reconciliation-required determinations are made; those remain Work Controller decisions.\"}"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,