{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CevkDcSepVJAVJaTrahTM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have completed the Independent Plan Review and returned it in the required structured format. The review is organized into the seven mandated sections, with each concern citing a specific artifact or repository-evidence anchor, stating the consequence, and giving the observation that would disprove it, while distinguishing demonstrated tensions from missing evidence.\n\nKey findings, in brief:\n\n- **Approach:** The plan's blanket `bad_request → TerminalError` conflicts with its own deliberate non-validation of caller-supplied numeric IDs — together they convert a user typo into an operational crash on the live emitter (the C1 conflict). The planner also still performs repairs (scope cleanup + normalization), so the \"no repair model\" premise is only partly true.\n- **Coverage gaps:** VC-POC-09/10 \"at least one filter beyond the sector default,\" `intent.filters` key whitelisting, and dual ownership of the teaching-staff alias are unaddressed.\n- **Architecture assumptions:** runtime input-catalog load for pinned static vocabularies, an unverified client catalog method, unverified production-path wiring, and the `deps.user_question` reliance that contradicts \"deterministic from intent.\"\n- **Testability:** exit-code-only `-k` gates can pass vacuously; several \"fail closed\" outcomes are ambiguous; and freezing the O-8 `xfail` is an implicit, unstated requirement creating an unsurfaced two-path divergence.\n- **Blind disposition:** Q1/Q4/Q8 resolved; Q2/Q3/Q6/Q7 partial; Q5 unanswered.\n\nAll decisions on materiality, blocking, and whether reconciliation is required remain with the Work Controller."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2956,"cache_read_input_tokens":154330,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m